%N A399466 Irregular triangle T(n, k), n >= 0, k = 1..A005942(n), read by rows; the n-th row lists the earliest starting offsets of the A005942(n) distinct subwords of length n in the Thue-Morse sequence (A010060).
%C A399466 Every nonnegative integer appears in the sequence (as A010060 is not ultimately periodic).
%H A399466 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399466/b399466.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10200</a>
%H A399466 Daniel Goc, Luke Schaeffer and Jeffrey Shallit, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.5352">The Subword Complexity of k-Automatic Sequences is k-Synchronized</a>, arXiv 1206.5352 [cs.FL], Jun 28 2012.
%H A399466 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399466/a399466.gp.txt">PARI program</a>
%F A399466 Empirically, T(n, A005942(n)) + n - 1 = A004759(n-2) for any n > 2.
%e A399466 Triangle T(n, k) begins:
